# Profile: baseline -- completely unmodified stock Chromium.
#
# The reference point for scripts/compare_builds.py on binary size, ISA content
# and benchmarks: generic x86-64, no microarchitecture targeting at all, which
# is what upstream ships.
#
# THIS FILE DELIBERATELY SETS NOTHING.
#
# It used to set use_znver5 = false and use_generic_avx512 = false explicitly.
# Those arguments do not exist in stock Chromium -- they are added by
# scripts/apply_zen5_patches.py -- and build.ps1 configure skips the patcher
# entirely for this profile. So on a freshly synced tree, where the patch has
# been discarded by `git checkout -f`, gn would hard-error:
#
#     Unknown build argument 'use_znver5'
#
# It only worked at all when a previous zen5 configure had left the patch in
# the tree, which is precisely the coupling this profile exists to avoid.
#
# Naming nothing is also correct on a tree that IS still patched: every
# argument the patch declares defaults to the value that reproduces stock
# behaviour, so a patched tree with none of them set compiles identically to an
# unpatched one. Either way this profile is stock, which is the whole point.
